        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 64-year-old male admitted on 19/04/2025 with an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia without significant hypercapnia. Spirometry confirmed severe airflow obstruction consistent with his known COPD. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a short course of systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone 40mg daily), and controlled supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with satisfactory clinical improvement. He was discharged on 20/04/2025 in stable condition. Please continue his usual inhaler regimen and arrange follow-up spirometry in 6 weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
